The plants above took every read of a kind at once. Taken out one at a time on TestKVPages_fusedKernelsReadTheTable alone, after the review (read 0 and 1 the keys, 2 and 3 the values; 0 and 2 the whole-run branch):
  attention_fa_blk read 0, 1, 2, 3: attention_fa_blk_g2, attention_fa_blk_g7 red each time
  attention_fa_blk64 read 0, 1, 2, 3: attention_fa_blk64_g7 red each time
That pass found a hole: at the full split count, 300 keys gave every chunk under 32 keys, so the kernel test never ran the whole-run branch, and a single read reverted there stayed green. The test now splits in two, which runs both branches. With a shipped read reverted, TestAttnFABlkIsTheGradedKernel goes red too.

